{"id":"bethabara","name":"Bethabara","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:bethabara"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Bethabara","text":"House of the ford, a place on the east bank of the Jordan, where John was baptizing (John 1:28). It may be identical with Bethbarah, the ancient ford of Jordan of which the men of Ephraim took possession (Judg. 7:24). The Revised Version reads “Bethany beyond Jordan.” It was the great ford, and still bears the name of “the ford,” Makhadhet ‘Abarah, “the ford of crossing over,” about 25 miles from Nazareth. (See BETHBARAH.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G2491","lemma":"Ἰωάννης","xlit":"Iōánnēs","gloss":"Joannes , the name of four Israelites","kjv":"John","count":3,"share":0.5},{"strong":"G2446","lemma":"Ἰορδάνης","xlit":"Iordánēs","gloss":"the Jordanes , a river of Palestine","kjv":"Jordan","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"G4008","lemma":"πέραν","xlit":"péran","gloss":"through","kjv":"beyond, farther  side, over","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"G907","lemma":"βαπτίζω","xlit":"baptízō","gloss":"to immerse, submerge","kjv":"Baptist, baptize, wash","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"G3699","lemma":"ὅπου","xlit":"hópou","gloss":"what where","kjv":"in what place, where, whither","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"G1563","lemma":"ἐκεῖ","xlit":"ekeî","gloss":"there","kjv":"there, thither, yonder","count":2,"share":0.33}],"verses":["John.1.28","John.10.40","John.10.41","Judg.7.24","John.10.39","John.10.42"],"related":[{"id":"herod","type":"lexical","strong":"G2491","why":"both lead with Ἰωάννης (G2491)"},{"id":"james","type":"lexical","strong":"G2491","why":"both lead with Ἰωάννης (G2491)"},{"id":"john","type":"lexical","strong":"G2491","why":"both lead with Ἰωάννης (G2491)"}],"works":[]}
